            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "content": "{{ states('input_text.bsb_dhw_once_status') }}\n\nNormal heating: **35–{{ states('sensor.bsb_normal_dhw_target_ceiling') }}°C**. Requests outside this limit are blocked. Presets start immediately."
            },
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "content": "Stops at the B3 target or saved timeout. Calendar and hourly top-ups wait during the cycle, then resume if enabled. Duplicate starts do not extend the deadline. Restart cancels an interrupted cycle; external setting changes release it and pause the calendar.\n\nThe request input accepts 20–75°C; the current native ceiling limits normal heating to 60°C. Native boiler control determines burner operation. B3 is a store probe, not tap temperature. Timed stops need Home Assistant and its connection."
            }
          ]
