            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "content": "{{ states('input_text.bsb_calendar_status') }}\n\n**Daily · 30 minutes every two hours**\n06:00, 08:00, 10:00, 12:00, 14:00, 16:00, 18:00 and 20:00.\n\nCircuit 1 enters **Protection between events** unless cold boost applies. Each event uses the return-water target above, currently 50°C. It can stop earlier at that cutoff; a slot does not force continuous burner firing. Automatic cycles **respect the room thermostat**. The override switch is for manual water cycles only.\n\n**Weather control:** at **25°C or above**, room heating is blocked. At **0°C or below**, cold boost allows extra cycles, including overnight when enabled. Thresholds are adjustable. Between these values, the normal daytime slots apply. Cold-boost cycles keep the return cutoff, maximum run time and ten-minute rest.\n\nThe Siemens room target is **18°C**; this is separate from water temperature. Home Assistant currently has no usable measured room temperature. The thermostat and native boiler controls remain responsible for room demand. Missing weather feedback blocks automatic heating; DHW and manual cycles remain independent.\n\n[Edit Heating events](/calendar) · Enabled schedules resume after restart checks; paused schedules stay paused."
            },
            {
              "type": "calendar",
              "entities": [
